  data:  # 6e0f
    kind: invariant  # 6e0f
    title: "META: AnalysisRun + behavior-map meta-layer writers have no validator"  # 6e0f
    status: violated  # 6e0f
    priority: 1  # 6e0f
    parent:  # 6e0f
    tags:  # 6e0f
    - dogfood_corpus_20260528  # 6e0f
    - dogfood_umbrella  # 6e0f
    - dogfood_severity_significant  # 6e0f
    - writer_contract  # 6e0f
    isbefore: []  # 6e0f
    duplicate_of: []  # 6e0f
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 6e0f
    pr_ref:  # 6e0f
    description: "**Origin.** Filed 2026-05-30 from the unlinked-investigation deep dive on 8 G4 items (notebookjournal_05302026_0411_unlinked_G4_metrics.md) plus 2 sibling items from G5 (notebookjournal_05302026_0411_unlinked_G5_axes.md sibling-pair-2). All ten items collapse onto one architectural shape: the behavior map's meta-layer has no writer contract.\n\n**The shape.** The serialized behavior map carries five families of meta-level structure — `analysis_runs[]`, `metrics`, `limits`, `config_fingerprint`, and per-record provenance fields on edges/nodes. Each family is wired by a different producer at a different pipeline stage with no cross-check. Symptoms split into four sub-patterns:\n\n1. **Schema declares, no writer wires.** Field exists in the dataclass, `to_dict()` serializes it, but no producer calls the writer. `Limits.add_classification_failure` (`limits.py:132`) has zero callers. `AnalysisRun.failed_files`/`warnings` are wired only on the analyzer base-class branch — orchestrator never aggregates analyzer-side warnings (e.g., the YAML \"173/174 files emit 0 nodes\" condition has no place to surface). Same shape as `edge.provenance`/`quality` empty (already-linked INV-nuzal) and `Edge.quality` always None (WI-lonoz).\n\n2. **Default-only initializer never overridden.** `AnalysisRun.create()` populates `config_fingerprint` with `_default_config_fingerprint()` (`ir.py:181`), which is literally `sha256(b'{}')`. Every analyzer and every linker uses `AnalysisRun.create(pass_id, version)` with no config arg, so all 84 runs collapse to the same fingerprint. Same producer-side independence drives `pass_version` empty on 44 analyzers (the `TreeSitterAnalyzer.pass_version` class attribute is never set; only linkers get `_stamp_pass_version` from `registry.py:656`), `toolchain` hardcoded to host Python via `_get_python_toolchain` (`ir.py:173`), and `analysis_runs[].skipped_passes` empty because `_filter_by_file_presence` writes only to `limits.skipped_passes` (`all_analyzers.py:151`).\n\n3. **Same name, two definitions across paths.** `total_io_edges` means `tagged_count` (pre-external_potential) at `io_boundary.py:1249` but `sum(len(e.chains))` (post-external_potential) at `cli.py:3870`. `metrics.total_files` is profile-sum, `unique_paths_in_analysis` is node-distinct-path — gap is 296. `metrics.compute_metrics` (`metrics.py:103-108`) creates `unknown` tier entries for edges whose src isn't in `node_id_to_tier`, producing the 23-edges-0-nodes phantom in `by_supply_chain_tier`.\n\n4. **Writer writes constant where schema reserves an evidence-derived slot (the 2.6 merged sub-pattern).** Schema field exists, writer DOES populate it, but with a hardcoded literal instead of an evidence-derived value. `Edge.confidence` is hardcoded per emitter (INV-suvil); `edge.provenance.derived_from` is empty across all edges where consumers expect a populated set (INV-nuzal). Distinguished from sub-pattern 1 (skipped writer) by symptom — null vs. constant — but the architectural gap is the same: no validator gates the writer.\n\n**Members at filing time (10).** INV-gizik, INV-jukok, INV-lidul, INV-mozaf, INV-nihug, INV-pitab, INV-pubom, INV-virik (G4); INV-suvil, INV-nuzal (G5, dogfood_writer_constant_face tagged). INV-nuzas joins as a near-sibling (tier-classifier failure consumes the missing classification provenance INV-virik should surface). Already-linked siblings outside the dogfood-66 corpus: WI-lonoz (Edge.quality null on self-analysis, already cross-refs INV-nuzal).\n\n**Why a META.** Any structural fix has to live above the individual writer sites — a property-test pass that loads `bm.json` and asserts (a) every schema field with a populated channel exists for every record, (b) named summary metrics agree across serialization paths, (c) every edge `src` resolves to a node id, (d) writer-side initialization-defaults never reach output, (e) emitters that populate evidence-derived slots use the derivation function not a constant. The umbrella exists because the test-pass change is one piece of work; the 10 member items are the regression cases it has to catch.\n\n**Fix shape.** New module `tests/test_behavior_map_writer_contract.py` (or analogous), wired to a fresh bm.json produced during CI. Each sub-pattern (1–4 above) becomes its own assertion class. Failing items become PRs against the producer of the field, not the test itself — each member item closes via a writer-side fix gated by the test."  # 6e0f
    fields:  # 6e0f
      statement: "Every field declared in the behavior map's meta-layer (analysis_runs[], metrics, limits, config_fingerprint, edge.src, provenance fields on edges/nodes) must be populated by some writer such that the value round-trips with the underlying record set across every producer."  # 6e0f
      root_cause: "The meta-layer was added incrementally without a single writer-contract owner. Producers wire fields independently at different pipeline stages — AnalysisRun.create() (ir.py:181-268), metrics.compute_metrics (metrics.py:103-108), Limits adders (limits.py:132-140), io_boundary tagging (io_boundary.py:1249) — and no validator stage asserts schema-conformance. Four symptom sub-patterns: (1) schema-declares-no-writer (INV-virik, INV-pitab partial), (2) default-only initializer never overridden (INV-lidul/INV-gizik/INV-nihug), (3) same-name two-definitions across paths (INV-pubom/INV-mozaf/INV-jukok), (4) writer-writes-constant where schema reserves evidence-derived slot (INV-suvil/INV-nuzal, tagged dogfood_writer_constant_face)."  # 6e0f
